^PXRMD(801.41,365,25,0)="^^2^2^3150710"
^PXRMD(801.41,365,25,1,0)="YES - reports military sexual trauma (MST) in the past"
^PXRMD(801.41,365,25,2,0)="      (answered 'YES' to AT LEAST ONE question)"
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,0)="^^17^17^3150710"
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,1,0)="Patient reports experiencing military sexual trauma (MST) in the past."
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,2,0)=" "
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,3,0)="The Veteran's subjective experience is sufficient for a positive screen. "
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,4,0)="Verification or additional detail is not necessary.  MST can occur on or "
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,5,0)="off base and while a Veteran was on or off duty. Perpetrators can be "
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,6,0)="anyone: men or women, military personnel or civilians, strangers, "
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,7,0)="friends, or intimate partners.  Examples of MST include a wide range of "
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,8,0)="unwanted sexual experiences, including offensive behavior or remarks, "
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,9,0)="unwanted sexual attention, or any unwanted sexual touching or other "
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,10,0)="activity that occurred while the Veteran was unable to refuse, coerced "
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,11,0)="(i.e. implied special treatment or hazardous duty or other negative "
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,12,0)="consequences), threatened, or forced. Physical force may or may not be "
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,13,0)="used and compliance does not indicate consent. All health care services "
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,14,0)="(inpatient, outpatient, and pharmaceutical care) for physical and mental "
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,15,0)="health conditions related to MST are provided free of charge."
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,16,0)=" "
^PXRMD(801.41,365,35,17,0)="   \\"
^PXRMD(801.41,365,100)="N"
