^PXRMD(801.41,10554,0)="VA-TEXT TDAP VHA GUIDANCE-PREGNANCY^^^E^^^^^^^1"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,1)="^^5"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,2)="^^1"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,0)="^^25^25^3160523"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,1,0)="PREGNANCY/BREASTFEEDING WOMEN\\"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,2,0)="1. Maternal vaccination. Health-care personnel should administer "
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,3,0)="   Tdap during EACH pregnancy, preferably during the third "
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,4,0)="   trimester (between 27-36 weeks gestation), although Tdap may be "
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,5,0)="   given at any time during pregnancy.  If not administered during"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,6,0)="   pregnancy, Tdap should be administered immediately postpartum.\\"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,7,0)="2. The rationale for repeat vaccination during EACH pregnancy is that   "
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,8,0)="   reported cases of pertussis continue to increase, uptake of"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,9,0)="   Tdap vaccine among pregnant women remains low and new data indicate"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,10,0)="   that maternal anti-pertussis antibodies are short-lived, thus Tdap"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,11,0)="   vaccination in one pregnancy will not provide high levels of "
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,12,0)="   antibodies to protect newborns during subsequent pregnancies. The"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,13,0)="   rationale for administration during the third trimester (between 27-36"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,14,0)="   weeks gestation) is that this would provide the highest"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,15,0)="   concentration of maternal antibodies to be transferred closer to birth,"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,16,0)="   but also allow for the 2 weeks (before birth) required to mount a"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,17,0)="   maximal immune response to the vaccine antigens.\\"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,18,0)="3. Pregnant women with unknown or incomplete tetanus vaccination. "
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,19,0)="   To ensure protection against maternal and neonatal tetanus,"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,20,0)="   pregnant women who never have been vaccinated against tetanus should"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,21,0)="   receive 3 doses of vaccine containing tetanus and reduced diphtheria"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,22,0)="   toxoids. The recommended schedule is 0, 4 weeks, and 6 through 12"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,23,0)="   months.  Tdap should replace 1 dose of Td, preferably between 27 and 36"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,24,0)="   weeks gestation to maximize the maternal antibody response and"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,25,25,0)="   passive antibody transfer to the infant.\\"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,100)="N^28"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,110,0)="^801.44D^1^1"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,110,1,0)="3160523.130624^54"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,110,1,1,0)="^^1^1^3160523"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,110,1,1,1,0)="Exchange Install"
^PXRMD(801.41,10554,110,"B",3160523.130624,1)=""
