^PXRMD(801.41,10688,0)="VA-DE VETERANS CHOICE TEMPLATE INSTRUCTION TEXT^^^E^^^^^^^1"
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,2)="^^1"
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,0)="^^38^38^3150106"
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,1,0)="The purpose of the Veterans Choice progress note is to communicate "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,2,0)="Veterans Choice appointment information and services approved. Its"
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,3,0)="primary purpose is for care coordination, but it is also to be used for "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,4,0)="attaching scanned documentation received from non-VA providers. "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,5,0)=" "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,6,0)="Responsible Staff: The Veterans Choice Note will primarily be completed by"
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,7,0)="Non VA Care staff involved in care coordination with the Veteran."
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,8,0)=" "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,9,0)="Sections: The Veterans Choice Note has two sections, the Pre-Visit and "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,10,0)="Post-Visit."
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,11,0)=" "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,12,0)="Pre-Visit Section: This section is used to document Veterans Choice "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,13,0)="Eligibility Type, Appointment Date and Time, non-VA provider, Approved "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,14,0)="Services, and any clinically pertinent information required for care "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,15,0)="coordination. "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,16,0)=" "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,17,0)="Eligibility Type: One Eligibilty type must be selected per visit. "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,18,0)="Eligibility determination information can be found at:"
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,19,0)="{FLD:VA-VETERANS CHOICE ELIGIBILITY INFO HYPERLINK}"
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,20,0)=" "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,21,0)="Post-Visit Section: This section is used to communicate that documentation"
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,22,0)="from the non-VA provider has been received and scanned into the medical "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,23,0)="record. It is also used to document any post appointment outcome "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,24,0)="information that is clinically pertinent and required for care "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,25,0)="coordination. "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,26,0)=" "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,27,0)="***The Post-Visit Section should be added as an addendum to the original"
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,28,0)="note that contains the Pre-Visit Information. Use the following "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,29,0)="instructions to open the VETERANS CHOICE NOTE template when making an "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,30,0)="addendum:"
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,31,0)=" "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,32,0)="1. Select the original completed VETERANS CHOICE NOTE from the list of "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,33,0)="completed notes on the Notes tab in CPRS.\\ "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,34,0)="2. Right click in the note text and select ""Make Addendum...""\\ "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,35,0)="3. When the blank Addendum opens, click on the ""Action"" menu above the"
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,36,0)="patient's name and click on ""Reload Boilerplate Text"".\\ "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,37,0)="4. The VETERANS CHOICE NOTE template will open.\\ "
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,25,38,0)="5. Select ""Post-Visit Information"" and complete as appropriate.\\"
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,100)="N"
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,110,0)="^801.44D^1^1"
^PXRMD(801.41,10688,110,1,0)="3150106.120323^17"
